# Dependencies
node_modules/
# package-lock.json is TRACKED deliberately. `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml` runs
# `npm ci` in its test job, and `npm ci` refuses to install without a committed
# lockfile — so ignoring the lockfile is why CI could never install jest. The
# test job is currently commented out by choice, so nothing runs `npm ci` today;
# committing the lockfile removes the blocker ahead of re-enabling it (US-001).

# Testing
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# Docs and tests are tracked deliberately:
# - __tests__/ must be committed or CI has nothing to run
# - docs/ holds the curriculum and methodology specs the app is built against

